  "title": "Film Connection Locations: Film School Near You",
  "content": "“I understand pre-sales and licensing now — and how to negotiate them.”\nWe have filmmaking professionals in cities throughout the U.S. Our professional directors, editors, cinematographers, screenwriters and producers will train you inside their film companies as an extern, teaching you many of the crucial technical skills you need to work in film. At the same time, you’ll also be paired with a professional director, producer or screenwriter who will help you develop your best idea for a great movie. You will then fly to L.A. or New York and pitch your idea to a studio, executive, or film producer who can get your movie made. They don’t call us revolutionary for nothing.\nFilm Production Programs and Courses for a new age. Learn, produce and share with the world in locations across the world.\nSelect any region from across the United States!\nSome of our graduates have gone on to become film directors, script writers, and production company owners. Others are creating and producing their own films across genres like documentary, drama, comedy, action, and animation\nNathan O.\n“This wasn’t just about being on set — it was about running one.”\nMichael N.\n“I didn’t realize how much tone depends on pacing until I was in the edit room.”\nBlake T.\n“Watching dailies with my mentor taught me to see the difference between what I imagined and what we shot.”\nSky R.\n“I thought pre-production was paperwork — now I see it’s where the film is born.”\nCasey T.\n“Craft services wasn’t just food — it was how I learned to read the crew’s needs.”\nJamie L.\n“I used to hate prep — now it’s my secret weapon.”\nMorgan K.\n“My mentor gave me tools to handle chaos without panicking.”\nPeyton T.\n“My mentor helped me rehearse investor meetings until I felt natural.”\nSkyler T.\n“I left with not just a project, but a plan to get it made.”\nCasey S.\n“I didn’t just get feedback — I learned how to give it to a room full of execs.”\nJesse T.\n“This course helped me connect creativity with long-term business thinking.”\nDrew F.\nFill out the form to reach a mentee advisor and learn about your opportunities.\n*Not all programs are available in every state. Consult a Mentee Advisor to learn more.",
